L35: 【13†FIZ Patmon】
L36: A CAS Registry Number^{®} includes up to 10 digits which are separated into 3 groups by hyphens. The first part of the number, starting from the left, has 2 to 7 digits; the second part has 2 digits. The final part consists of a single check digit.
L37: 
L38: The check digit is developed by following a standard calculation shown below. Use it to see if you have a valid CAS Registry Number.
L39: 【14†Image: Explanation of the CAS Registry Number check digit formula, worked through for 107-07-3.†cdn.prod.website-files.com】
